    "text": "A uniform circular loop of radius a and resistance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is pulled at a constant velocity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></math> out of a region of a uniform magnetic field whose magnitude is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>. The plane of the loop and the velocity are both perpendicular to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>. Then the electrical power in the circular loop at the instant when the arc (of the circular loop) outside the region of magnetic field subtends an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> at the centre of the loop is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/WhatsApp_Image_2020-06-20_at_3.30.18_PM.jpeg\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 185px;\" />",
